g opportunity  to bring off meta and and  situational picks that are going to be  relevant and tailored to the situation  you've collected information on  next up we've got the border rework look  as someone who actually hasn't been the  biggest fan  of how transformative the recent map  reworks have been  i gotta say i love love  this rework why because they barely  touched the map  it's not the the map became bad it's  that the game evolved the players  evolved the strat of all the the way we  play siege all together  is no different and that was exactly the  philosophy  for our level designer behind it like  keep the good stuff  and just tweak the the stuff that were  not completely working right  they massaged the parts that needed  massaging in this case opening up  showers and creating a connector between  securities and top east stairs  and leaving virtually everything else  intact i really  really hope they adopt this same  approach for future reworks  like bank speaking of map reworks  ubisoft revealed that as part of their  2021 road map  they'd be taking a second crack at  favela  and thank the [ __ ] lord outback  they also announced some really exciting  stuff in terms of operator reworks  for starters they're making it so that  melusi's mines are going to be a  shitload easier to destroy  they're also removing the shield portion  of goyo's deployables leaving just this  kind of shrouded explosive  making his area denial a lot less  oppressive ubisoft also teased that  later in the year we'd be seeing reworks  of  mira maestro finca and fuse  now i don't know about you but i am  madly excited about these reworks  a future in which my boy fuse is viable  is the future i want my children to grow  up in  but of all the things that crimson heist  has bestowed upon we the students of  siege  none are as holy as hallowed as the fact  that we can finally watch a [ __ ]  replay that's right siege's match replay  system is  finally entering beta i cannot oversta